description:
What: Add PinningApiKey newtype wrapper that redacts itself in Debug and Display output, preventing accidental credential logging.

Algorithm:
1. Create crates/transit/src/retention/remote_pin_client.rs (new module, also home for the RemotePinClient in e0v.4)
2. Define:
   pub struct PinningApiKey(String);
   impl PinningApiKey {
       pub fn new(key: impl Into<String>) -> Self { Self(key.into()) }
       pub(crate) fn as_bearer_header(&self) -> String {
           format!("Bearer {}", self.0)
       }
   }
   impl std::fmt::Debug for PinningApiKey {
       fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {
           write!(f, "PinningApiKey(<redacted>)")
       }
   }
   impl std::fmt::Display for PinningApiKey {
       fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter) -> std::fmt::Result {
           write!(f, "<redacted>")
       }
   }
3. Add pub mod remote_pin_client; to crates/transit/src/retention/mod.rs
4. ExternalPinServiceConfig's api_key should be converted to PinningApiKey after loading from config (not stored as PinningApiKey in the serde-deserialize struct — keep it as String there for TOML parsing, convert to PinningApiKey in the service initialization code)

Defensive programming:
- The inner String is not pub — only as_bearer_header() exposes it (in the Authorization header)
- as_bearer_header() is pub(crate) — not exposed outside the retention module
- No From<PinningApiKey> for String — prevents accidental leakage
- Implementing PartialEq is FORBIDDEN to prevent timing attacks (use constant-time comparison if needed)
